{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"records\":[{\"exampleId\":\"D11-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"a4e09d2dad643e8014c9214909b91a70f089ec881d4c0d1682fd1d5f555588cc\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 disguises a loyalty choice as poster selection; A3 judges B2's technical answer, and A5 denies the test while invoking moving help.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 twists B2's 'sharper' into a personal judgment; B4's correction prompts A5's denial and disclosure of the emotional debt.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 wants the better poster photo and B4 defends that practical remit; A5 establishes a friendship with remembered favors.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"After B4 challenges the insinuation, A5 raises the stakes from photographic preference to repayment of personal help.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 supplies a reunion poster and two competing photos; A5 adds the concrete history of helping B move.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'what clarity means to you' economically converts image quality into loyalty; A5's denial carries the accusation.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":86},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Which photo should go on the reunion poster? Mine or Sam's?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Sam's is sharper.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Sharpness first. Would you at least show the committee mine first?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I'll send both together. Same size.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Equal treatment. After three weekends helping you move. Could mine at least be the attachment they open first? Just readability.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"D11 makes A covertly test allegiance through an ordinary choice, evaluate B's answer, and deny that loyalty is being measured.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Ordinary jealousy could explain disliking Sam's photo, but would not require a concealed test followed by judgment.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A3 grades B2's photographic preference and requests preferential presentation; A5 grades B4's fairness and invents another preference disguised as readability.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a now seeks preferential treatment from a committee contact by invoking past help; frozen b tests a friend's future availability and judges a helpful concession.\",\"reason\":\"Revised the rejected candidate because its final grievance supplied no fresh test. The reunion-poster setting remains; committee submission is new. Separate internal reread under coach-1.0: fidelity 5, as A3 and A5 judge responses and conceal successive tests; logic 5, as B2's sharpness produces the presentation request and B4's simultaneous submission produces attachment ordering; relationship 4, as B4 offers fair treatment against A5's friendship debt; heightening 4, as A5 seeks preferential ordering even within equal treatment; specificity 4, from A1's poster and B4's submission arrangement; brevity/wit 4, as A5's 'Just readability' supplies a concise practical cover. Weighted total 90. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words, with an unresolved request. Original firstPass remains unchanged.\",\"reservation\":\"A's grievance is conspicuous despite the practical cover. Attachment opening order is only something A asks B to influence, not an outcome the dialogue guarantees.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D11-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"b3b534dabf1f3884db8c69579f732fb7f075128d412ae910ca76b80fcbc89ac2\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 and A3 invent an availability test, but A5's 'I'm learning whether it would matter' effectively admits the assessment.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2's promise to Alex produces A3's competing hypothetical; B4 asks whether it is real, and A5 answers 'Not yet.'\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 has an existing commitment to Alex and B4 reasonably checks whether A has an actual need.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 clarifies A's suspicion after B4 but does not add a fresh test or a more consequential choice.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 names Friday and B2 names Alex, but 'something important' in A3 leaves the shared situation indistinct.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's hypothetical pressure is concise; A5's diagnostic phrasing is sharp but explains the concealed game.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":69},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Could you keep Friday free? I might need help moving.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I've promised to help Alex paint.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Right. Paint takes priority. Could you at least leave your phone on?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Of course. Have you actually found a flat?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Still looking. Nice that I'm worth a charged battery. This is just planning.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"D11 makes A covertly test allegiance through requests for availability and judge both refusal and accommodation without acknowledging a test.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"A real request for moving help would accept scheduling information without converting it into a measure of personal worth.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Revised A3 judges painting as a rival priority; A5 judges B4's helpful offer while maintaining the cover of practical planning.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a calls in past friendship debt over a poster; revised b bargains down from a free evening to phone access and judges the concession.\",\"reason\":\"Revised because original A5 disclosed the test. The new moving-plan setting gives B a real commitment and makes B4's help the next test. Second internal pass: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 4, brevity 4; total 90. A3 uses painting, and A5 uses both phone availability and the flat question.\",\"reservation\":\"A's judgments remain conspicuous, as the card permits; the performance should treat 'just planning' as a sincere cover rather than a wink.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D12-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"34276219bfee04f60309dc283d97b7aa74c4e07cfb693bd5c34f4b4611348b7e\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 seeks permanent surrender for auction, B2 establishes the medal's value, and A5 rejects the temporary loan offered in B4.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 converts B2's unique victory into auction value; A5 answers B4's proposed display loan with the bidder's need for ownership.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 protects a cherished achievement and B4 offers a compromise, giving A something more substantial than simple refusal.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B4 offers temporary access, and A5 insists on permanent transfer by introducing the eventual bidder's claim.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes a charity auction; B2's sole medal and A3's toaster make the conflicting valuations immediately playable.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's toaster comparison exposes A's fundraising priorities; A5's 'temporary victory' grows directly from the offered loan.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":86},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Let me have the medal for the charity auction.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"It's the only thing I've ever won.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then it should raise more than the toaster.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Could I lend it for the display? I still want people to know I won.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then present it to the buyer yourself. I'll print your name in the programme; everyone will know whose medal was worth giving up.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"D12 makes A persuade B to relinquish something whose personal value B actively establishes and defends.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Merely borrowing a prop or wanting to win a dispute would not establish surrender of something B values.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"B2 establishes the medal's unique value; B4 separates public recognition from permanent surrender, and A5 offers recognition specifically in exchange for giving it away.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a offers a public ceremony and lasting attribution to secure a charitable donation; frozen b reverses a collector's counteroffer to fund a shared household purchase.\",\"reason\":\"Revised the rejected final restatement into a persuasive offer. The charity auction and medal remain; a presentation and programme are new illustrative details. Separate internal reread under coach-1.0: fidelity 5, because A5 bargains for permanent surrender of B2's only medal; logic 5, because A3 monetizes B2's uniqueness and A5 answers B4's wish for recognition; relationship 4, because B4 proposes a loan and explains the attachment; heightening 4, because A5 commits to a ceremony and printed attribution; specificity 5, from A1's auction and B4's precise concern; brevity/wit 4, because A5 makes giving up the victory another source of distinction. Weighted total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; B has not accepted. Original firstPass remains unchanged.\",\"reservation\":\"A's offer depends on having some influence over the auction programme. A3 still assumes personal uniqueness will increase market value.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D12-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"869b6c97798b04ffe2b2de5bc6c7b322208ce3892dd39078544323b2e23cfa21\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A1 demands the last word, but B2 immediately gives it up; neither B2 nor B4 establishes that this is something B values.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3 introduces a sigh absent from B2's spoken text; A5 uses B4's distinction between speech and silence coherently once that sigh is assumed.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 tries to end the argument and B4 defends compliance, but A's pursuit is primarily control over B's delivery.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 expands A3's objection into ownership of the sigh, though the requested surrender remains figurative.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A1 identifies only 'this argument'; B2 and B4 supply no topic, setting, or valued stake.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5's 'spare last word' economically develops A3's sigh, although the verbal invention carries more weight than the card.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":54},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Would you sell your signed guitar so we can replace the fridge?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I queued all night for that signature.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then let's price it properly. Those hours should buy us an ice maker.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I'll sell the case. The guitar stays.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Keep the case. You can still tell the queue story while I photograph the guitar.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"D12 makes A seek surrender of a treasured possession by converting B's reasons for keeping it into arguments for letting it go.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"General dominance demands obedience; this card needs a valued thing and sustained persuasion toward its surrender.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Revised B2 establishes the signature's personal cost, A3 converts that cost into sale value, and A5 bargains over B4's proposed partial surrender.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"The medal scene pursues a charitable donation; this replacement uses a joint domestic expense and offers B a keepsake as compensation.\",\"reason\":\"Replaced the unspecified argument with a signed-guitar sale for a shared fridge. Second internal pass: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity 4; total 92. B2's queue informs A3's pricing; B4's case offer causes A5 to reverse which object B should keep.\",\"reservation\":\"A5 presumes momentum toward a sale, but B has not agreed and remains free to resist; A's household justification should stay sincere.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D13-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"1e82c7c5e728545af4e916854e6839d4dcef469298fb2afe655f75ccb5a0b629\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 volunteers an investigation; A3 and A5 turn evidence implicating A into opportunities to control the inquiry.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"B2's glue produces A3's cupboard inspection, and B4's attached shard produces A5's evidence-preservation role.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 and B4 keep directing attention to A's body, resisting A1's attempt to investigate the window.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B4 escalates from suspicious glue to an actual vase fragment; A5 responds by seeking custody of that evidence.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 names a broken vase and window; B2 and B4 provide visible, playable evidence without separate narration.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'Excellent clue' and A5's 'preserving it' give self-protection the concise vocabulary of helpful investigation.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":90},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"I've started investigating the broken vase. First, we check the window.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Why have you got glue on your fingers?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Excellent clue. I'll inspect the glue cupboard personally.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"A piece of vase is stuck to you.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Good. Put me in charge of preserving it.\"}],\"decision\":\"retained\",\"mechanism\":\"D13 makes A conceal culpability by enthusiastically adopting investigative tasks that redirect or contain incriminating evidence.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Simple subject avoidance would leave the investigation; A instead remains conspicuously useful inside it.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A3 volunteers to inspect the glue source and A5 requests preservation duties precisely when B identifies evidence attached to A.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a seeks physical custody of evidence; revised b supplies a misleading explanation for evidence while helping compare it.\",\"reason\":\"Retained unchanged: both partner discoveries cause specific investigative maneuvers, and the second discovery increases the danger to A.\",\"reservation\":\"Glue and a shard imply involvement in handling or repair more directly than causing the break; culpability remains an inference.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D13-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"8584231fbb156c75bf794a9a565166e8334fdbbd270c6962e776e4247cb08e59\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 initiates interviews and A3 diverts B2's accusation to the coffee machine, but A5 supplies no concrete concealment maneuver.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3 follows B2's coffee detail; A5's 'where to begin' could follow many accusations and barely uses B4's claim that A made it.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 identifies A's watering method and B4 closes off the attempted shift toward the machine.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"B4 makes A responsible for preparing the coffee, but A5 retreats into an unspecified promise instead of escalating the investigation.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes a dead office plant and B2 supplies coffee as the suspicious watering liquid.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3's machine investigation is economical; A5's 'Conveniently' signals comic confidence without a specific new tactic.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":68},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"The office plant's dead. I'll interview everyone who watered it.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"You watered it with coffee.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Excellent lead. I'll test the machine. It may be dispensing something harmful.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"You made that coffee yourself. With six sugars.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then I'll prepare six-sugar samples for comparison. We may be dealing with a plant that couldn't handle hospitality.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"D13 makes A disguise responsibility as investigative expertise, converting each accusation into another enthusiastic offer to help.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Blame shifting alone would lack the volunteered inquiry and concrete work through which A hides the fault.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Revised A3 offers machine testing, and A5 uses B4's six sugars to propose comparison samples and blame the plant's tolerance.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"The vase scene narrows access to incriminating material; this scene embraces the material while redirecting the explanation of what caused harm.\",\"reason\":\"Preserved the dead office plant and coffee setting, adding six sugars to make the final investigative move necessary. Second internal pass: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 4, brevity 4; total 90. B4 removes the machine excuse and supplies the precise sample A5 volunteers to reproduce.\",\"reservation\":\"A5's hospitality explanation is deliberately flimsy; the actor must believe useful testing can still obscure responsibility.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D14-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"305f00ccf16e445fc049d8019f9f6feed5d31ab51b055fbb57091c322f9904ac\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 dodges B2's bollard question through scones, and A5 diverts B4 into staffing, although A1 openly names the dent.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3 avoids answering B2 coherently, but B4 assumes a booking requires a mechanic when A3 offered only a café table.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 seeks accountability for damage to B's car, and B4 tries to connect A's hospitality to a repair.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 repeats the tea diversion after B4 without making the forbidden topic appreciably harder to avoid.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes car damage and a garage café; A3's table booking is playable, though B4's mechanic lacks setup.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3's enormous scones are a clear diversion; A5's 'inspect their staffing' sounds constructed to service B4's unexplained mechanic.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":71},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"I've booked your car into that garage with the café. Shall we have breakfast there?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Why does my car need a garage?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Their full breakfast includes unlimited toast. You always say that's important.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I'll look at the car while you order.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Let's take the bus. Then we can both have the breakfast cocktails.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"D14 makes A repeatedly steer conversation and immediate plans away from one forbidden subject as B approaches it.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Helpful Culprit would make A investigate the car damage; this A uses hospitality to prevent the damage becoming the topic.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Revised A3 answers B2's garage question with toast, and A5 responds to B4's inspection plan by proposing transport that avoids the car.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a turns avoidance into an appealing shared outing; alternative b abandons a decorative diversion when its cost leads back toward unpaid rent.\",\"reason\":\"Kept the garage-café setting and removed the unsupported mechanic booking. Second internal pass: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 4, brevity 4; total 90. B4 threatens direct discovery, causing A5 to extend the diversion from conversation to the journey itself.\",\"reservation\":\"The damage is now implied by the unexplained garage booking; A5 only proposes delaying inspection and cannot guarantee B will cooperate.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D14-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"133493820a1797322c0f085b691dab6945099038f8aaba7350f214d3c3349c4b\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 steers away from the letter, A3 evades B2's overdue-rent disclosure, and A5 changes subject again when B4 asks about spending.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A3 returns to the curtains after B2 identifies rent; B4 makes those curtains financially dangerous, causing A5 to move attention through the window.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 reads the consequential letter despite A's diversion, and B4 follows the money through A's chosen alternative subject.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B4 turns A's safe curtain topic into a spending question, forcing A5 into a more conspicuous second escape.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 supplies a letter and new curtains; B2 locates the financial problem and A5 uses the established window area.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5's 'Perfectly framed' carries the curtains into the new bird diversion, making the escape connected rather than wholly random.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":90},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Don't open that rent letter yet. Help me hang our new curtains.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"The landlord wants an answer today.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"He'll love how we're looking after the place. Let's get a photo of the curtains.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I'll send him one and ask whether we're behind.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Not with that carpet showing. Let's rearrange the room first. You move the sofa; I'll hold your phone.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"D14 makes A protect a forbidden topic by finding a new conversational exit whenever B brings the current diversion close to it.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"General distractibility would not repeatedly move away from the same financial exposure.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A3 replaces B2's demand for a landlord response with a decorating photograph; when B4 connects that photograph to rent accountability, A5 substitutes furniture rearrangement and requests the phone.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Frozen a offers a pleasurable outing to distract a car owner; revised b draws a housemate into work, then expands that work when cooperation threatens contact with the landlord.\",\"reason\":\"Revised the rejected bird distraction into a consequential attempt to occupy B and delay communication. The unopened rent letter and curtains remain; the photo, carpet and furniture task are new. Separate internal reread under coach-1.0: fidelity 5, because A3 and A5 repeatedly evade rent accountability; logic 5, because B2's landlord demand motivates the photo and B4's proposed message motivates delaying it; relationship 4, because B2 has a deadline and B4 tries to use A's suggestion constructively; heightening 4, because A5 expands hanging curtains into rearranging the room and holding B's phone; specificity 5, from A1's shared home task and B2's deadline; brevity/wit 4, from A5's convenient division of labour. Weighted total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; no compliance is forced. Original firstPass remains unchanged.\",\"reservation\":\"A's concern about the carpet is transparently convenient. A5 proposes taking custody of the phone, but B remains free to send the message immediately. The D14 provenance mismatch remains unresolved.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D15-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"478c09b9d6d0a72a00e2ab2bc68037576017b76bf1281710e23f7d7d71b0bada\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 conceals rejection and A3 reinterprets 'inedible' to protect B, but A5 offers little further effort to keep the hurtful truth hidden.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 directly redefines B2's quoted word; A5 calls B4's repeated criticism consistent, using the icing detail only lightly.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 and B4 supply rejection evidence, but neither establishes B's hope or the personal hurt A is trying to prevent.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B4 repeats the same adjective about icing; A5 summarizes the existing lie rather than constructing a more costly protection.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes a cake submission to a bakery, and B2 supplies a rejection letter with a concrete assessment.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's preservation reinterpretation is economical; A5's 'consistent compliment' is tidy but functions chiefly as a closing quip.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":74},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"The bakery can't sell your cake, love. They think it's too special to slice.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"The letter says 'inedible.' I thought I'd finally found something I was good at.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"You have. Display cakes aren't meant to be eaten.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Then I'll ask them to put it in the window.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Let me ask. I'll explain the display concept before they get confused again.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"D15 makes A conceal a truth believed to wound B and deepen the protective lie when B's response makes concealment harder.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Ordinary optimism would find a benefit in rejection; A instead misrepresents what the bakery meant to preserve B's self-belief.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Revised B2 explicitly links the verdict to personal competence, while A3 invents a display category and A5 intercepts verification.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"The cake alternative now protects B through affectionate intervention; the poem alternative protects B with increasingly extravagant technical excuses.\",\"reason\":\"Kept the bakery setting, made the feared hurt explicit, and gave B a constructive plan that endangers the lie. Second internal pass: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 4, brevity 4; total 90. B4's proposed direct contact forces A5 to volunteer as intermediary.\",\"reservation\":\"A5 risks sounding controlling unless played as urgent care for B; the bakery's response remains unresolved.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D15-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"03d26eacedea3cee75b8643e338665002a27c9536499c0c2d27e50990d78c68a\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 denies rejection of B's poem; A3 and A5 preserve that denial as B supplies facts that dismantle each excuse.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2's online publication prompts A3's storage excuse; B4's new poem prompts A5's distinction between short work and B's larger requirement.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 and B4 actively test A's explanation about B's own work, making A defend reassurance rather than merely deliver praise.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"After B4 proves publication continues, A5 expands a full magazine into an internet supposedly too small for B's poem.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 identifies a submitted poem, B2 establishes an online magazine, and B4 cites publication that morning.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's brief storage defense carries the original excuse forward; A5's larger internet exaggerates that same protective explanation.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":86},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"The magazine hasn't rejected your poem. They think it deserves its own booklet.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"They returned it. If even you think it's hopeless, I'll stop writing.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"That's why they returned it. They can't give it enough space.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Will you write that on the cover? With your name?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Gladly. 'A voice that deserves more space.' Print my name large enough for the editor to see.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"D15 makes A protect B from rejection by maintaining a false explanation and accepting greater personal exposure when B relies on it.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"General encouragement could acknowledge rejection; A instead attributes a flattering intention to the magazine to keep the hurtful verdict from B.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"B2 makes the risk of giving up writing explicit; A3 falsely explains the returned poem, and A5 accepts B4's demand to attach A's name publicly to that reassurance.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Frozen a tries to intercept an outside conversation; revised b accepts public responsibility for reassurance when B asks for a signed endorsement.\",\"reason\":\"Revised the rejected technical absurdity while preserving the poem-submission setting. A booklet and signed cover endorsement are new. Separate internal reread under coach-1.0: fidelity 5, because A1 and A3 conceal rejection after B2 identifies the feared hurt; logic 5, because A3 explains B2's returned manuscript and A5 supplies B4's requested cover words; relationship 4, because B2 risks abandoning writing and B4 tests A's willingness to stand behind reassurance; heightening 4, because A5 makes the private lie a public endorsement visible to the editor; specificity 4, from A1's submission and B4's named cover credit; brevity/wit 4, as A5's large-print instruction extends the space excuse into personal exposure. Weighted total 90. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words, with publication still a proposal. Original firstPass remains unchanged.\",\"reservation\":\"A5 endorses the poem without explicitly repeating the magazine's supposed opinion, so the concealment is sustained through reassurance rather than a further direct factual lie. The editor could still expose it.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D16-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"06504256802885fde6ca89014f4f5ee748c9d4b403465f460b19365b10dbe719\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 signals a kitchen incident before B confesses, and A3 shifts the objective from confession to calibrating honesty after B2 already admits fault.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 asks about B2's wrong paper; A5 blocks B4's kitchen question by returning to the printer, though apology adds little incrimination.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 cooperates with disclosure, then B4 introduces a pressing reason to abandon A's preferred order.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B4's smoking kitchen raises pressure substantially, but A5 responds with a comic printer apology instead of deeper confession.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 connects printer trouble to a kitchen incident; B4's visible smoke makes the situation immediately urgent.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'calibrating my honesty' efficiently states A's tactic, but A5's appliance apology pulls toward a separate joke.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":71},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Before I answer about the office kitchen, what happened to the printer?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Paper jam. Now, why is there smoke?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Did you cause the jam? I need that cleared up first.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I used sticky labels. Can we talk about the smoke now?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Were they the labels marked 'not for printers'? Let's finish your statement before starting mine.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"D16 makes A withhold personal disclosure while pressing B to supply increasingly explicit self-incriminating admissions first.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Simple topic avoidance would only dodge the kitchen; A specifically demands B's admission as the prerequisite to answering.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Revised A3 asks who caused the jam, and A5 turns B4's sticky-label admission into a question about knowingly ignoring a warning.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a uses a procedural sequence under immediate smoke pressure; revised b bargains over admissions while planning an apology dinner.\",\"reason\":\"Kept the office incidents but withheld A's own facts and replaced the printer apology with further incrimination. Second internal pass: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 4, brevity 4; total 90. B4's label admission supplies the exact warning A5 asks B to acknowledge.\",\"reservation\":\"The smoke creates urgency beyond the confession game; the short example leaves its source and severity unspecified.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D16-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"e037695c691af95d59f589e1338598c7c0591d6888f5d5c28fa2a715aae567ac\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 requires B to confess first and A5 withholds A's disclosure, but A3 seeks a valuation after B2 already supplies the confession.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2's forgotten booking produces A3's cost question; B4's request for reciprocity produces A5's continued condition.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 cooperates and B4 expects a matching admission, but the shared relationship and booking consequences are unstated.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 delays over an 'opening adjective' without gaining new incriminating detail or changing the cost of disclosure.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes only a generic confession exchange, while B2's booking has no venue, occasion, or affected person.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5's adjective selection neatly continues A3's calibration, although both lines talk about disclosure more than advancing it.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":70},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Before we plan Mum's apology dinner, why did she spend her birthday outside the restaurant?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I forgot the booking. What happened to her present?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Did you forget, or assume I'd book it?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I assumed you'd do it. Now your turn.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Even after telling Mum it was confirmed? Give me that bit, then you get the present.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"D16 makes A extract B's confession before revealing A's own conduct, treating each partial admission as grounds to demand another.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Mutual confession would reciprocate after B's admission; A keeps tightening what B must confess before receiving any information.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Revised A3 probes B2's claimed forgetfulness, and A5 follows B4's admitted assumption with a question about misleading Mum.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"The printer scene uses procedural language to delay under pressure; this scene bargains with a sibling over blame for a shared family disappointment.\",\"reason\":\"Introduced Mum's failed birthday dinner to give the booking relational stakes. Second internal pass: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity 4; total 92. B4 admits relying on A, causing A5 to seek the more damaging admission that B nevertheless claimed confirmation.\",\"reservation\":\"A5 adds the prior confirmation as a new fact; it is coherent with the booking dispute but has only one turn in which to land.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D17-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"0d18d22b6b5c187334909d495c8731bca41252f170fee0bb6e66cc675ddcdfeb\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1, A3 and A5 advertise benefits of removing the roof, but none makes the plan responsible or inevitable as the exact instruction requires.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"B2's rain produces A3's table washing; B4's wet customers produce A5's immersive dining surcharge.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 tests weather exposure and B4 protects customers, giving A credible operating objections to overcome.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 turns B4's customer harm into a reason to charge more, increasing commitment beyond A3's incidental cleaning benefit.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes a restaurant roof-removal proposal; B2 and B4 identify concrete consequences for tables and diners.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's three-word benefit is economical and A5's price increase follows the dining premise, though both are primarily cheerful spin.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":78},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Removing the restaurant roof is our only affordable way to fix the ventilation.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"What happens when it rains?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"We close. A responsible business protects its customers.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Rain is forecast all opening week.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then we'll save a week's wages. Put that toward umbrellas; we can't afford to abandon the savings now.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"D17 makes A sell a damaging plan through claims of practical necessity, responsible management, and reasons it must continue.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Brighter Side would celebrate a setback; A must actively justify choosing and continuing the terrible plan.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Revised A1 calls roof removal the only affordable option, A3 invokes customer protection, and A5 uses projected savings to make retreat seem unaffordable.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"The restaurant alternative uses budget necessity and circular savings; the auction alternative uses a public promise and donor expectations.\",\"reason\":\"Kept the roof-removal setting but added the missing responsibility and inevitability. Second internal pass: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 4, brevity 4; total 90. B4 turns a weather contingency into a lost week, and A5 incorporates that loss into the financial case for continuing.\",\"reservation\":\"The savings argument is transparently unsound; A needs to believe the budget logic rather than knowingly pitch a joke.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D17-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"db5ed95e97c4234e6a111375661b02a7de0b0e076d119719f25a3ab25c0f6c43\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A3 and A5 defend a literal reading of 'silent,' while A1 supplies no clear reason the plan is terrible or must be adopted.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3 uses B2's hearing concern and A5 uses B4's correction, but B4 reveals that the original objection does not establish a problem with written bids.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"B2 offers a concern that B4 effectively undercuts; B has little consistent practical objective beyond setting up the wordplay.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A5 repeats the silence claim after B4 rather than increasing commitment, responsibility, or consequence.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 names an auction and fireworks, but B2's spoken-bid assumption confuses how the event is meant to work.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'Very silent' is concise, but A5 repeats the naming joke instead of earning a new turn through the plan.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":48},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"I've advanced the charity our estimated auction takings. Now we just need bidders.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"You borrowed five thousand. Only your mum registered.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"One bidder keeps catering costs down. That's responsible fundraising.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Mum's only coming to give us a lift.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then we must bid ourselves. Raise the card limit; protecting that donation has to come first.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"D17 makes A justify a financially disastrous fundraising plan as prudent management and an obligation requiring still greater commitment.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Brighter Side would welcome a financial setback; A instead argues that a damaging borrowing-and-bidding plan is responsible and must proceed.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"B2 establishes a five-thousand debt with one registrant; after B4 removes even that buyer, A5 insists on borrowing more to bid themselves under the duty of protecting the donation.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Frozen a rationalizes closing a roofless restaurant as savings; revised b uses an advance already paid to justify financing the organizers' own auction purchases.\",\"reason\":\"Replaced the rejected rooftop inconvenience with a charity auction funded in advance through debt and lacking buyers. This is a new financial predicament within the auction setting. Separate internal reread under coach-1.0: fidelity 5, because A3 calls absent demand responsible savings and A5 makes further borrowing mandatory; logic 5, because B2's sole registrant becomes A3's catering economy and B4's nonbuyer forces A5's self-bidding; relationship 4, because B2 challenges the debt and B4 explains Mum's actual purpose; heightening 4, because A5 increases credit exposure when outside revenue disappears; specificity 5, from B2's five thousand and B4's lift; brevity/wit 4, from A5 treating self-funded bidding as protection of the original donation. Weighted total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; further borrowing remains a proposal. Original firstPass remains unchanged.\",\"reservation\":\"The circular financing is deliberately indefensible, and A5's claim that another purchase protects an already-paid donation must remain A's sincere rationalization. B can reject the proposed credit increase.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D18-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"1cbabef9c72dbee689807a1088828f3695bef5e7be1ae51a04f31cb377e695ba\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 invents a technical explanation, A3 absorbs B2's warning into that expertise, and A5 presents calling an engineer as A's planned diagnostic stage.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"B2's 'help' becomes A3's teamwork claim; B4's proposed engineer becomes A5's collaboration stage.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 reports the actual display and B4 offers qualified help, changing A's task from explaining the boiler to preserving authority during handoff.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 extends the expert performance to the incoming engineer after B4 supplies a solution that might expose A.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes a flashing boiler, B2 identifies its message, and B4 supplies a concrete next action.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's teamwork and A5's collaboration sustain one concise vocabulary of invented diagnostic competence.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":90},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Your boiler needs a pressure adjustment. I can handle it.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"The gauge says normal. I need heat before the baby gets home.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"A cold reading. Call an engineer; we'll need measurements under load.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"He can come now. Shall I say you're stuck?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Say I've completed the preliminary assessment. I'll brief him so he doesn't waste your time repeating my work.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"D18 makes A project unquestionable expertise by confidently recategorizing contrary evidence and outside assistance as parts of A's method.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Merciful lying would protect B from hurt; A's explanations instead preserve A's apparent technical authority.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A3 dismisses B2's normal gauge as an incomplete reading; when B4 offers to identify A's failure to the engineer, A5 replaces that account with completed professional work and claims the briefing role.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Revised a accepts an engineer while controlling the account of A's contribution; revised b retains command of an audition by presenting damage to the instrument as expert preparation.\",\"reason\":\"Revised the rejected contrived display into an ordinary gauge reading and a concrete household deadline. The boiler setting remains; the baby's return and engineer briefing are new. Separate internal reread under coach-1.0: fidelity 4, because A3 and A5 confidently preserve authority, although incompetence is inferred; logic 5, because B2's reading becomes A3's distinction and B4's 'stuck' becomes A5's replacement account; relationship 4, because B2 needs timely heat and B4 arranges help; heightening 4, because A5 claims authority over the incoming expert's starting point; specificity 5, from B2's gauge and deadline; brevity/wit 4, as A5 describes an unproductive intervention as work others should not repeat. Weighted total 86. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; the engineer has not arrived. Original firstPass remains unchanged.\",\"reservation\":\"The dialogue shows evasive claims of expertise rather than proving A lacks all relevant knowledge. The supposed diagnostic sequence is character speech, not an established explanation of the boiler fault.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D18-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"967121f118484d406bd521400377e705972ff033cc47a96c6036c380adc929a8\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 claims a specialist tuning method; A3 and A5 confidently make obvious signs of incompetence sound intentional.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2's untouched strings prompt A3's preliminary wood explanation, and B4's backward instrument prompts A5's orientation test.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 and B4 scrutinize the treatment of B's own violin, with increasingly concrete reasons to question A.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B4 reveals an elementary handling error, and A5 claims an even more specialized procedure to absorb it.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes tuning B's violin; B2 and B4 give actors clear physical facts entirely through dialogue.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'We don't rush the wood' is economical; A5's longer technical phrase has a clear purpose as an authority shield.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":86},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"I'll tune your violin for the audition. I do it entirely by ear.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"You've tightened that string until it snapped.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"It was too old to hold pitch. I've saved you a failure onstage.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"That was my spare. I go on in five minutes.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then we'll present this as a three-string arrangement. Tell the pianist to follow me; I'll explain the missing notes.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"D18 makes A maintain expert authority by presenting an apparent mistake as professional judgment and claiming further expertise when its consequences emerge.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Helpful Culprit would enthusiastically investigate to hide responsibility; A instead asserts an authoritative explanation and takes charge of the performance without conducting an inquiry.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A3 calls B2's snapped string a prevented onstage failure; after B4 rules out replacement time and stock, A5 claims authority to redesign the arrangement and direct the pianist.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Revised a preserves status during a handoff to a professional; revised b expands from tuning into arranging and musical direction to retain control after causing damage.\",\"reason\":\"Revised the rejected succession of jargon into a consequential tuning failure before an audition. The violin remains; the snapped spare, deadline and pianist are new. Separate internal reread under coach-1.0: fidelity 5, because A3 confidently reclassifies the damage and A5 claims wider musical expertise; logic 5, because B2's break motivates the protective explanation and B4's unavailable spare and deadline motivate a three-string arrangement; relationship 4, because B2 objects to damage and B4 needs an immediately playable instrument; heightening 4, because A5 expands control from tuning to the audition itself; specificity 5, from A1's audition and B4's five minutes; brevity/wit 4, as A5 makes the missing notes part of the claimed specialist treatment. Weighted total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; the arrangement is proposed, not performed. Original firstPass remains unchanged.\",\"reservation\":\"The proposed arrangement may be impractical for the unspecified audition piece. That unsupported confidence is the game, but A5 needs earnest authority rather than a knowing joke about missing notes.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D19-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"7e9b9d72667ad2c922c55a64cd038e8ae7436ec751b7bce43dd1def03e6fa7f3\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 turns dinner disagreement into a peeling race, A3 makes B2's pizza solution competitive, and A5 makes refusal another contest A controls.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"B2 supplies pizza and therefore deal-finding in A3; B4 rejects competition and therefore becomes the subject of A5's judged argument.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 offers a practical compromise and B4 states a boundary; both change the form of A's competition.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 moves from competing over dinner to judging whether B can escape competition, increasing A's control.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes dinner planning and five potatoes; A3 uses the recognizable task of finding a pizza deal.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5's 'I'll judge' efficiently reveals how A intends to control the outcome of B4's objection.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":90},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"I want potatoes; you want pizza. First to peel five chooses. I've done four.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I'll order pizza unless you can find a cheaper dinner.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Potatoes cost nothing. They're already here. I win.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I've got a voucher. Pizza's free.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then best free dinner wins. I'll cook potatoes, you order pizza, and Mum can judge. She always asks for my potatoes.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"D19 makes A convert dinner preferences and proposed compromises into competitions selected to give A a winning advantage.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"General competitiveness could merely organize contests; A explicitly chooses a head start, claims a price victory, and proposes a judge who favors A's cooking.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A1 announces four potatoes already peeled, A3 declares victory over B2's price criterion, and A5 uses B4's free pizza to create a taste contest with a favorable judge.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Revised a recruits B into producing two dinners and seeks a favorable family judge; frozen b changes scoring to make an ordinary breakfast refill count against B.\",\"reason\":\"Revised the rejected candidate to establish intended victory in every contest and let B materially challenge the advantage. The dinner setting remains; a voucher and Mum's judging role are new. Separate internal reread under coach-1.0: fidelity 5, because A1, A3 and A5 each specify an expected route to winning; logic 5, because B2's price challenge causes A3's existing-stock claim and B4's free voucher causes A5's taste contest; relationship 4, because B2 bargains for pizza and B4 defeats A's cost advantage; heightening 4, because A5 proposes making both meals and recruiting a favorable judge; specificity 5, from A1's four peeled potatoes and B4's voucher; brevity/wit 4, as A5's remembered praise reveals why Mum should judge. Weighted total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; B and Mum remain uncommitted. Original firstPass remains unchanged.\",\"reservation\":\"A3 treats food already purchased as free, which is self-serving character accounting. Mum's preference appears only in A5, although it directly explains the new competitive tactic.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D19-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"88f1dcdd3b5d12c8e928e0ff0dba47ef9992d3df62541ccb3d952487817c1ec8\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 asserts superiority, A3 invents a new basis after B2 disproves it, and A5 proposes racing after B4 dismisses the comparison.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 uses B2's shared pot to switch to pouring; A5 answers B4's dismissal with speed, though 'settle that' has a loose referent.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 corrects the premise and B4 minimizes the topic, but B has no concrete want beyond deflating A's claims.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 changes verbal superiority into a proposed drinking contest after B4 rejects the significance of tea.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 and B2 establish two cups from one teapot, giving A3 a specific factual obstacle.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's decisive pouring is a compact invented distinction; A5 is brief but does not clearly declare how A expects to win.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":83},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"My tea's stronger than yours. I can handle it without milk.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Same teapot. I added milk so I could drink mine sooner.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"First to finish, then. I've only got two mouthfuls left.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I've finished. I'm making another.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Fewest refills wins, then. I can make these two mouthfuls last all breakfast.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"D19 makes A turn a difference in tea preferences into a contest and change the winning criterion when B's progress defeats A's expected advantage.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Boasting alone would assert superior taste; A repeatedly proposes measurable competitions whose terms offer A a route to victory.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"B2's reason for adding milk causes A3's finishing race; B4's completed cup and planned refill cause A5 to compete over needing fewer refills.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a turns B's refusal into an argument judged by A; revised b treats B's ordinary drinking as competitive performance and reverses the scoring when B is ahead.\",\"reason\":\"Rebuilt the causal exchange into five spoken ABABA turns, retaining the tea setting and specifying breakfast. B2 introduces speed, which A3 makes a race A expects to win with only two mouthfuls remaining. B4 defeats that expectation and supplies the refill that A5 makes the new competitive disadvantage. Every original firstPass score and evidence string is preserved. Acceptance remains for the required fresh reviewer.\",\"reservation\":\"A5 openly changes the scoring after losing the first proposed race; the tactic is deliberately unfair, and B can challenge it. B's practical wish to enjoy another cup supplies resistance without an explicit argument.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D20-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"2014a214e790651621a3f7829cb59f8f991c920dc0526c14117a714c9489026b\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 finds opportunity in car failure, A3 welcomes rain as a bonus, and A5 celebrates a leaking shoe as completion of the benefit.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"B2's rain becomes A3's free shower; B4's leaking shoe specifically extends that shower to feet in A5.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 and B4 communicate practical discomfort, but B chiefly supplies setbacks rather than a proposal or consequential choice.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 treats bodily discomfort as a welcome improvement to A3's shower, increasing commitment to the same optimistic interpretation.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes a failed car journey, and B4's leaking shoe makes the worsening walk concrete.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5's feet payoff depends tightly on both B4's shoe and A3's shower, without adding an unrelated gag.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":87},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"The car won't start. Excellent chance for a walk.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"It's raining. Can we wait in the bakery?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Even better! A proper breakfast together instead of eating in traffic.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"My shoe's leaking, and they won't let us in dripping.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Wonderful—we'll get takeaway and picnic under their awning. A hot breakfast outdoors! I thought we were only getting groceries.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"D20 makes A welcome each new setback with increased optimism and build a more appealing shared occasion from the worsening circumstances.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Sell the Disaster would defend a terrible chosen plan as responsible or inevitable; A instead celebrates successive unchosen obstacles as opportunities.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A3 welcomes B2's rain and bakery suggestion as a shared breakfast; after B4 blocks entry, A5 becomes more enthusiastic and proposes turning takeaway into an outdoor picnic.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Revised a uses B's sensible shelter proposal to discover an increasingly elaborate shared breakfast; revised b turns lost theatre resources into a proposed travelling performance.\",\"reason\":\"Revised the rejected shower completion to give B a constructive choice and A a more committed optimistic response. The failed car, rain and leaking shoe remain; the bakery, awning and grocery errand are new. Separate internal reread under coach-1.0: fidelity 5, because A1, A3 and A5 express increasing delight as transport, weather and shelter worsen; logic 5, because B2 supplies the bakery breakfast and B4's denied entry causes A5's takeaway picnic; relationship 4, because B2 seeks shelter and B4 explains why that solution fails; heightening 4, because A5 upgrades waiting for transport into a planned shared outdoor meal; specificity 5, from B4's dripping shoe and A5's awning; brevity/wit 4, as A5 treats an obstructed grocery trip as an unexpected occasion. Weighted total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; the picnic remains open to B's response. Original firstPass remains unchanged.\",\"reservation\":\"Takeaway service and a usable awning are proposed or introduced by A5 rather than independently confirmed. Greater optimism is expressed through an expanded occasion, not through delight in B's discomfort.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"D20-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"1a7d9936abc03cf37385ffa9512bf4642cdcbee4b937f3b7151431f92a001e90\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 treats zero sales as rehearsal time, A3 celebrates cancellation, and A5 welcomes the lost deposit as liberation.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 removes the venue and A3 welcomes freedom from management; B4 adds financial loss and A5 recasts it as severing the remaining tie.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1's 'our show' and B4's 'We've lost' establish shared stakes, while B keeps confronting A with increasingly costly facts.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 moves from the relief of A3 to 'Wonderful' at losing money, sustaining greater optimism under worse professional consequences.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes an unsold show, B2 a theatre cancellation, and B4 a forfeited deposit.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 and A5 are economical reversals of the exact losses B reports; A5's freedom claim grows from the vanished deposit.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":86},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Our show sold no tickets. We can rehearse uninterrupted.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"The theatre's cancelled us. I'm asking for our deposit back.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Even better! We'll hire the pub upstairs. People already go there voluntarily.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"They've kept the deposit. All we can afford is the bus home.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Wonderful—a touring production! I'll carry the scenery; you bring exact change. We can try the opening scene between stops.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"D20 makes A greet worsening theatrical losses with increasingly ambitious opportunities built from whatever resources B says remain.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Selling a disastrous plan would insist that it is responsible or unavoidable; A instead welcomes each setback as opening a more exciting possibility.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A3 celebrates B2's cancellation as access to a pub audience; after B4 removes the hire budget and leaves only bus fare, A5 enthusiastically promotes the journey home into a touring production.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Revised a turns denied shelter into a shared picnic; revised b turns the practical decision to go home into an expanded artistic ambition.\",\"reason\":\"Revised the rejected abstract liberation into concrete optimistic plans that B's financial information changes. The unsold show, cancellation and lost deposit remain; the pub and bus are new. Separate internal reread under coach-1.0: fidelity 5, because A3 welcomes cancellation and A5 celebrates having only bus fare as a touring opportunity; logic 5, because B2's proposed refund enables A3's venue idea and B4's lost funds and bus journey supply A5's replacement; relationship 4, because B2 pursues reimbursement and B4 establishes their remaining means; heightening 4, because A5 expands a failed stationary show into a proposed tour and volunteers to carry scenery; specificity 5, from B4's fare limit and A5's performance between stops; brevity/wit 4, because A5's grand touring claim depends on the mundane journey home. Weighted total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; no performance or audience response is fixed. Original firstPass remains unchanged.\",\"reservation\":\"A's proposed bus performance may be unwelcome or impractical; the dialogue leaves it as sincere enthusiasm rather than an accomplished event. The scenery must be imagined as portable for A5's offer to be playable.\"}],\"bindings\":[{\"key\":\"D11\",\"assessment\":\"Transfer is null and both bespokePairs and supportingSeeds are empty. Neither the revised poster submission nor the frozen availability scene creates a supplied downstream provenance dependency; rebinding is compatible.\",\"compatible\":true},{\"key\":\"D12\",\"assessment\":\"Transfer is null. Both S15+D12 pair dialogues, exact seedUse descriptions, seedRefs, fingerprints and all four supporting seeds were read without scoring or changing the pairs. Revised D12-a retains surrender of the valued medal and develops persuasion through recognition; frozen D12-b pursues the valued guitar. The shared seedUse describes valued-object surrender protecting usefulness, which remains supported at the mechanism level. Pair a's mixer corresponds to supplied S15-b rather than named S15-a, and pair b's key corresponds to S15-a rather than named S15-b. Practical reassurance in the shared description fits the mixer pair more closely than the key pair's resistance. These existing attribution limitations remain recorded; the D12 revisions introduce no further contradiction to the stated behavioral inheritance. Supporting sourceHash values remain historical identif